From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arkun <jstn.lucas@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:26:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] SpruceMOSS-3326: resolve RK3326 boards from the device
 tree

spruce resolved every RK3326 board to Pixel2 (cpuinfo part 0xd04). The
SpruceMOSS-3326 RK3326 image names its board in device-switch's group
node, rocknix,device_switch/this (rk3326-device-group-twig.dtsi in the
twig fork), so read it: g350 -> G350. Anything else - no node, as on
twigUI's own Pixel 2 image, or a board without a platform yet - stays
Pixel2. The stderr redirect comes before the input redirect so a missing
node prints nothing under dash, bash or busybox sh.

The new boards run the Pixel 2's twig userspace and the emulators twig
builds for its image, so:
- device_names: G350 answers to BATLEXP_G350 and then GKD_PIXEL2, the
  Pixel 2's name doubling as the twig RK3326 family token (the
  ANBERNIC_RGXX pattern) - no Emu config.json needs editing.
- Every branch that is about twig's userspace rather than the Pixel 2's
  hardware takes G350 and XUMiniM too: file manager, gallery and reader
  gptokeyb maps, PortMaster's PYSDL2 path, boot-logo conversion skip,
  advmame, drastic (dispatches run_drastic_$PLATFORM), OpenBOR, PICO-8,
  ScummVM (shares the pixel2 config), RetroArch --config, firstboot's
  advmame unpack, the tz-data timezone exemption, theme loading screen.
  XUMiniM is listed ahead of its platform; nothing resolves to it yet.

The updater is left alone: it only uses PLATFORM to pick the Mini
startup or the Flip session, and both RK3326 boards take runtime.sh.
